[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
I inspected OSPF across the campus core and distribution devices and found no ongoing adjacency flapping. On every core router (router7, router8, router16, router17, router10, router11, router1), OSPF neighbors are Full with stable dead timers and clean interface counters. Examples:
- router7 shows Full with router1 (192.168.10.2) on eth2, router10 (192.168.144.1) on eth3, router16 (172.30.1.1) on eth4, and router8 (172.25.1.2) on eth5; each reports “State is Full … 6 state changes” with the last change several minutes ago and no retransmit queues.
- router8, router16, router17, router10, router11, and router1 report the same—neighbors Full and 6 prior state changes, last change minutes ago. Interface stats on the suspect links (e.g., router7 eth5 to router8 eth4; router7 eth4 to router16 eth2) show zero errors/drops.
- mswitch0 and sshswitch do run OSPF (ospfd present, OSPF routes installed), but logs show only initial bridge/port transitions at startup; no recurring link flaps.

